Maybe this world is another planet's Hell. Begin doing what you want to do now. We are not living in eternity. We have only this moment, sparkling like a star in our hand and melting like a snowflake. Everything has been figured out, except how to live. Thank you for sending me a copy of your book - I'll waste no time reading it. A doctor can bury his mistakes but an architect can only advise his clients to plant vines. He is one of those people who would be enormously improved by death. Those who are willing to sacrifice essential liberties for a little order, will lose both and deserve neither. Talent does what it can; genius does what it must. The only difference between me and a madman is that I'm not mad. I do not feel obliged to believe that the same God who has endowed us with sense, reason, and intellect has intended us to forgo their use. Education is a progressive discovery of 
 our own ignorance. The ultimate measure of a man is not where he stands in moments of comf
 ort and convenience, but where he stands in times of challenge and controversy. Opportunity is missed by most people because it is dressed in overalls and looks like work. Compassion is the antitoxin of the soul: where there is compassion even the most poisonous impulses remain relatively harmless. I have come to believe that the whole world is an enigma, a harmless enigma that is made terrible by our own mad attempt to interpret it as though it had an underlying truth. Good people do not need laws to tell them to act responsibly, while bad people will find a way around the laws. Egotist: a person more interested in himself than in me. Love is the energy of the soul. Love is what heals the personality. There is nothing that cannot be healed by love. There is nothing but love. First they ignore you, then they laugh at you, then they fight you, then you win. A little inaccuracy sometimes 
 saves a ton of explanation. We have art to save ourselves from the truth. His ignorance is
  encyclopedic Never interrupt your enemy when he is making a mistake. Change is inevitable, except from vending machines. Maybe this world is another planet's Hell. Touch is the most fundamental sense. A baby experiences it, all over, before he is born and long after he learns to use sight, hearing, or taste, and no human ever ceases to need it. Keep your children short on pocket money - but long on hugs. You can't wait for inspiration. You have to go after it with a club. Distance between two hearts is not an obstacle; rather a great reminder of just how strong true love can be. Only two things are infinite, the universe and human stupidity, and I'm not sure about the former. Books are the shoes with which we tread the footsteps of great minds. Do, or do not. There is no 'try'. If you can't get rid of the skeleton in your closet, you'd best teach it to dance.Not all chemicals are bad. 
 Without chemicals such as hydrogen and oxygen, for example, there would be no way to make 
 water, a vital ingredient in beer. The difference between 'involvement' and 'commitment' is like an eggs-and-ham breakfast: the chicken was 'involved' - the pig was 'committed'. The use of COBOL cripples the mind; its teaching should, therefore, be regarded as a criminal offense. Beer is proof that God loves us and wants us to be happy. If you want to make an apple pie from scratch, you must first create the universe. Blessed is the man who, having nothing to say, abstains from giving us wordy evidence of the fact. Too often we give our children answers to remember rather than problems to solve. Books are the shoes with which we tread the footsteps of great minds. If you are going through hell, keep going. Life's challenges are not supposed to paralyze you, they're supposed to help you discover who you are. Moral indignation is jealousy with a halo. No elected body is the country, we ar
 e the country. You and me. Us. It can only stay that way as long as we care to keep it so.
  Sleep is an excellent way of listening to an opera. Anyone who considers arithmetical methods of producing random digits is, of course, in a state of sin. Only two things are infinite, the universe and human stupidity, and I'm not sure about the former. One of the symptoms of an approaching nervous breakdown is the belief that one's work is terribly important. Why is it drug addicts and computer afficionados are both called users? A kiss is a lovely trick designed by nature to stop speech when words become superfluous. How wrong it is for a woman to expect the man to build the world she wants, rather than to create it herself. Thank you for sending me a copy of your book - I'll waste no time reading it. Logic is in the eye of the logician.Life is a waste of time, time is a waste of life, so get wasted all of the time and have the time of your life. You can widen your life by yourself, 
 but to deepen it you need a friend. All truth passes through three stages. First, it is ri
 diculed. Second, it is violently opposed. Third, it is accepted as being self-evident. Anyone who considers arithmetical methods of producing random digits is, of course, in a state of sin. All truth passes through three stages. First, it is ridiculed. Second, it is violently opposed. Third, it is accepted as being self-evident. When we drink, we get drunk. When we get drunk, we fall asleep. When we fall asleep, we commit no sin. When we commit no sin, we go to heaven. So, let's all get drunk and go to heaven! I begin by taking. I shall find scholars later to demonstrate my perfect right. God, please save me from your followers! Friends are as companions on a journey, who ought to aid each other to persevere in the road to a happier life. Love takes up where knowledge leaves off. Love is composed of a single soul inhabiting two bodies. The optimist proclaims that we live in the best of 
 all possible worlds, and the pessimist fears this is true. All are lunatics, but he who ca
 n analyze his delusion is called a philosopher. Give me a museum and I'll fill it. You can't be a real country unless you have a beer and an airline. It helps if you have some kind of a football team, or some nuclear weapons, but at the very least you need a beer. 24 hours in a day, 24 beers in a case. Coincidence? Sometimes our light goes out but is blown into flame by another human being. Each of us owes deepest thanks to those who have rekindled this light. Too often we give our children answers to remember rather than problems to solve. It's not that chocolates are a substitute for love. Love is a substitute for chocolate. Chocolate is, let's face it, far more reliable than a man. Each problem that I solved became a rule which served afterwards to solve other problems. Compassion is the antitoxin of the soul: where there is compassion even the most poisonous impulses remain relative
 ly harmless. Everything has been figured out, except how to live. It's kind of fun to do t
 he impossible. No matter what looms ahead, if you can eat today, enjoy today, mix good cheer with friends today enjoy it and bless God for it. We all agree that your theory is crazy, but is it crazy enough? If we had no winter, the spring would not be so pleasant; if we did not sometimes taste of adversity, prosperity would not be so welcome. Obstacles are those frightful things you see when you take your eyes off your goal. A positive attitude will not solve all your problems, but it will annoy enough people to make it worth the effort. I'd rather have a bottle in front of me than a ... brain operation. We didn't lose the game; we just ran out of time. A woman drove me to drink and I didn't even have the decency to thank her. You can widen your life by yourself, but to deepen it you need a friend. Each encounter that becomes a friendship turns into a lifeline. One can never have too ma
 ny, only too many to properly take care of. Without question, the greatest invention in th
 e history of mankind is beer. Oh, I grant you that the wheel was also a fine invention, but the wheel does not go nearly as well with pizza. The quality of the moment is more important than the number of our days. A human being should be able to change a diaper, plan an invasion, butcher a hog, conn a shp, design a building, write a sonnet, balance accounts, build a wall, set a bone, comfort the dying, take orders, give orders, cooperate, act alone, solve equations, analyze a new problem, pitch manure, program a computer, cook a tasty meal, fight efficiently, die gallantly. Specialization is for insects. Always do sober what you said you'd do drunk. That will teach you to keep your mouth shut. Of cheerfulness, or a good temper - the more it is spent, the more of it remains. Nothing splendid has ever been achieved except by those who dared believe that something inside them was superior 
 to circumstances. Your living is determined not so much by what life brings to you as by t
 he attitude you bring to life; not so much by what happens to you as by the way your mind looks at what happens. What lies behind us and what lies before us, are only small matters compared to what lies within us. 

